# Dependencies — restored with `npm install`
node_modules/

# Build output — produced by `npm run build`, `npm run build:single`
# and `npm run app:build`
dist/
dist-single/
dist-app/

# Scrumly's own data is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# Point the Local folder setting at this repo and scrumly.json, plus the dated
# files under history/, are versioned along with the code. Every task, sprint
# and blocker then has a full history, and `git log` answers "when did this
# change" for the data as well as for the app.
#
# Two things to know before relying on that:
#
#   - Notes are in there, including one-to-one notes marked private. Git history
#     is permanent, so anyone you ever add to this repo can read them, and making
#     the repo public would expose them. Keep it private, or keep the folder
#     somewhere else.
#   - Nothing commits automatically. The file is rewritten seconds after any
#     change, so the working tree will usually show it as modified; committing
#     is still yours to do.

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Claude Code's local tooling config. Kept on disk so the dev server still
# starts from here, just not carried in the repo.
.claude/
